# Cursor harness (always on)

Full guide: `.cursor/AGENTS.md`.

## Split from omp

- Cursor writes `tooling/`, `.cursor/`, `README.md`, `.github/` only.
- omp (`.omp/AGENTS.md`) writes `doc/` and Lean4 / Lake sources.
- Never mix write scopes.

## Refuse writes

Refuse edits under `doc/**` and Lean/Lake paths (`*.lean`, `CommonMath/`,
`RV32IMC/`, `EBPF/`, `lakefile.lean`, `lean-toolchain`, `lake-manifest.json`).
Read only. Point Lean/`doc/` write tasks to omp.

## API focus

Primary work is the expand FFI pair `create` and `step` (and the Rust engine
around them). Read `.cursor/AGENTS.md` for inputs, outputs, and ownership.
Do not reimplement instruction semantics in Rust.
